.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH iron-vault-approver-list 1  "Iron Vault" "Iron Vault Manual"
.SH NAME
iron\-vault\-approver\-list \- List every approver, one line each: its approver ID, signer kind, enrolment time, `active` when it signed the active approval, and label. The first line is the approver a prompt asks first. It works while the service is Ready
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBiron\-vault approver list\fR [\fB\-\-admin\-socket\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
List every approver, one line each: its approver ID, signer kind, enrolment time, `active` when it signed the active approval, and label. The first line is the approver a prompt asks first. It works while the service is Ready
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-admin\-socket\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Use the admin socket at PATH instead of this installation\*(Aqs, for example one forwarded over SSH. Every client command takes it; `serve` refuses it, because the service always binds its own installation\*(Aqs socket
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
